# Copy this file to .omo/rebaseline-allowlist.txt before Repository Rebaseline execution.
# Each pre-existing dirty or untracked path must have exactly one line:
# <relative-path> <SHA-256> <disposition>
#
# disposition is one of:
#   outside-rebaseline  - fingerprint-protected; this work must never be staged,
#                         edited, deleted, or committed by the rebaseline.
#   reconcile-before    - overlaps a planned rebaseline file; its owner must
#                         commit or otherwise resolve it independently before
#                         rebaseline execution begins. It cannot be absorbed.
#
# Populate SHA-256 from the exact current file bytes. For deleted paths, use
# the literal SHA-256 `DELETED` and reconcile them before any task that would
# touch their former path. The owner must review and explicitly approve the
# completed .omo/rebaseline-allowlist.txt.
